## The 3-tier taxonomy (the binding rule)

{{SYSTEM_NAME}} tokens live in three variable collections, layered. **Components bind to tier 3 only.**

| Tier | Collection | Mode(s) | Role | Bind in production? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `1. Primitives` | `Value` | raw values — full color ramps, spacing/typography primitives | ❌ never bind directly |
| 2 | `2. Tokens` | `Value` | numeric/sizing tokens with semantic naming (`Border-Radius/*`, `Border-Width/*`) + aliased color tokens | only numeric tokens (no Semantic tier exists for numbers) |
| 3 | `3. Semantic` | `Light` (+ `Dark` when added) | role-named colors (`Surface/*`, `Text/*`, `Icon/*`, `Border/*`) | ✅ **always** for colors |

**Rules:**
- Bind every visible fill/stroke color to a **`3. Semantic`** token — never a primitive or raw hex.
  The clue: role names (`Surface/Border/Text/Icon`) are tier 3; color-ramp names (`Color/Primary/700`)
  are tier 1/2.
- Bind spacing / radius / sizing to **`2. Tokens`** number variables (`Scale/*`, `Border-Radius/*`,
  `Border-Width/*`) — numbers have no Semantic tier.
- Theme with **variable modes** on `3. Semantic` (add a `Dark` mode), not parallel `*/Inverse` tokens.
- Variable IDs are stored as `VariableID:<n>:<m>` (e.g. `VariableID:26:24`). The `VariableID:` prefix is
  REQUIRED for `getVariableByIdAsync` — see `figma-gotchas.md` Gotcha #29.

