## Binding patterns (system-agnostic — keep)

```javascript
// Color variable binding (needs a fallback paint — Gotcha #11)
function bindFill(node, variable) {
  const modeId = Object.keys(variable.valuesByMode)[0];
  const val = variable.valuesByMode[modeId];
  const fallback = (val && val.r !== undefined) ? val : { r: 0, g: 0, b: 0 };
  node.fills = [figma.variables.setBoundVariableForPaint(
    { type: "SOLID", color: fallback }, "color", variable
  )];
}

// Numeric binding — note the API field-name inconsistency
node.setBoundVariable("paddingTop", scale400);
node.setBoundVariable("topLeftRadius", borderRadiusMd);   // NOT radiusTopLeft
node.setBoundVariable("strokeTopWeight", borderWidthSm);  // NOT topStrokeWeight

// Text style binding (async)
await textNode.setTextStyleIdAsync(style.id);
```

## Honest binding hierarchy

1. **Prefer Semantic over Token over Primitive** — always.
2. Colors → the role token that matches the surface (text on `Text/*`, fills on `Surface/*`, etc.).
3. Numbers → `Scale/*` (padding/gap), `Border-Radius/*` (radii), `Border-Width/*` (stroke weights).
4. Never ship literal hex or literal numbers where a token exists.

